<worksheet >
    <title>EIPO-4 Orthogonality</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete both problems. 
      Complete problem 1 with progress on problem 2 to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
      <exercise>
        <p>Given the set of vectors <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="1">
          <mrow>v_1=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}\\\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}\\\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}\end{bmatrix},
    v_2=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{-\sqrt{2}}{2}\\0\\\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\end{bmatrix},
    v_3=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{\sqrt{6}}{6}\\\frac{-\sqrt{6}}{3}\\\frac{\sqrt{6}}{6}\end{bmatrix}</mrow>
        </md> Determine whether this set of vectors is orthogonal, orthonormal, or neither. Support your answer.</p>
      </exercise>
    </page>
    <page>
      <exercise>
        <p>Compute the orthogonal projection of 
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="1">
            <mrow>u= \begin{bmatrix}4\\-1\end{bmatrix}</mrow></md> onto the line through 
            <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="1">
              <mrow>v= \begin{bmatrix}-1\\1\end{bmatrix}</mrow></md> and the origin.</p>
      </exercise>
    </page>
</worksheet>